=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  logforward review-several ------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Decided: no Figma frame. Set servers with three servers in$
# hardn.yml: a Server row each, one file with an action and a$
# queue for each, one check, one restart, one test line. The$
# question counts them.$
$
  Checking the host...$
$
# Set servers ##################################################$
$
# Note$
# Every message the host logs goes to each server, as it is$
# logged.$
$
  Forwarding ---------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Server               logs.example.net:6514 TLS$
   -  CA File              /etc/ssl/lab-ca.pem$
   -  Server               192.0.2.51:514 TCP$
   -  Server               192.0.2.52:514 UDP losses unseen$
$
   -  Write hardn's forwarding file$
      /etc/rsyslog.d/60-hardn-forward.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,17 @@$
      +# Written by hardn (Syslog Settings).$
      +*.* action(type="omfwd" protocol="tcp"$
      +    target="logs.example.net" port="6514"$
      +    StreamDriver="gtls" StreamDriverMode="1"$
      +    StreamDriverAuthMode="x509/name"$
      +    StreamDriverPermittedPeers="logs.example.net"$
      +    StreamDriver.CAFile="/etc/ssl/lab-ca.pem"$
      +    queue.type="linkedList" queue.timeoutEnqueue="0"$
      +    action.resumeRetryCount="-1")$
      +*.* action(type="omfwd" protocol="tcp"$
      +    target="192.0.2.51" port="514"$
      +    queue.type="linkedList" queue.timeoutEnqueue="0"$
      +    action.resumeRetryCount="-1")$
      +*.* action(type="omfwd" protocol="udp"$
      +    target="192.0.2.52" port="514"$
      +    queue.type="linkedList" queue.timeoutEnqueue="0"$
      +    action.resumeRetryCount="-1")$
      $ rsyslogd -N1$
$
   -  Restart rsyslog$
      rsyslog$
      $ systemctl restart rsyslog$
$
   -  Send a test line$
      $ logger -t hardn "log forwarding set"$
$
  Forward logs to 3 servers? [y/N, 0 or q]: $
$
$

